    verification recallSecondHopRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "8da1e1d1-8a95-4de0-8229-7f35e0489cb0"; :>> title = "Sprint 593 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "READY, and the scope changed once during refine on evidence. The frontier's top item had failed three sprints, so the first act was to diagnose rather than to build: a per-component ranking dump showed the two remaining hand-set misses are not one problem but two. The rebase question's d0129 sits at rank 63, reached at two hops, behind a top row scoring 31.5 against the second's 17.1 - the exact shape of the one mechanism the criterion named and nobody had tried. The obligation question's d0176 is not reached at all, and issue391 already records why and puts the measurement-definition question to the human. So this sprint takes the reachable half and leaves the definition question where it is: 7/8 clears the bar without touching ground truth, which is the outcome issue391 hoped for and could not assume. Sized 3: a research loop with a measurement cycle of several minutes and an unknown number of iterations, which is not a 2."; }
