    verification recallSecondHopImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "30704f34-f295-4b63-8b7b-424c9b1d141d"; :>> title = "Sprint 593 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "RAN, in this order, because the order is the method. Diagnosed first with a component dump behind KEEL_RECALL_DEBUG, which is what turned 'not shown' into 'rank 63, own score only'. Wired the KEEL_RECALL_* knobs both harnesses have passed through since D0325 and nothing had read. Swept the mechanism on the default arm: six configurations, all identical to off - the arm cannot see a second hop, which became D0364 and issue405. Built the two-hop arm and swept there against a rule fixed before the sweep; took DOMINANCE 1.25 as the strongest setting that costs the near arm nothing. Only then ran recall_ab.py: 7/8. Extracted the score fold into rank_reached and the dump into dump_ranking when clippy's line limit refused the function, which left it better than it was. Unit test pins both halves of the mechanism - the dominated chain carries its two-hop neighbour, the flat field gets nothing."; }
    // RAN: keel suite 570 passed 0 failed (receipt 91238ffbf2c6); recall_bench.py 49/50@13 and --hops 2 22/50; recall_ab.py 7/8 x3; validate 674; guard ALL PASS; clippy clean
    part recallSecondHopImplementGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "523433ba-767e-4064-bc5a-a50a25042f52"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "018315ace003b7751ab5cb31f5ab653f2faa58bf"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }
    verification recallSecondHopReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "2d8ea5d8-7d65-40f1-9bd4-13a0db06f0af"; :>> title = "Sprint 593 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "THREE PASSES per D0172. (1) IS THE NUMBER HONEST: the 7/8 was read after the choice, not before, and the parameters were not touched afterwards - that sequence is the whole value of the result and it is recorded in D0365 in the order it happened. The one-hop arm's top-three placements fall 30/49 to 28/49, which the pre-stated rule did not cover; it is written into the Decision's consequences rather than left out. (2) DID I FIT ANYTHING TO THE HAND SET: no, and the temptation was concrete - DOMINANCE 1.1 and 1.0 score far better on the two-hop arm and would very likely have carried the hand set higher, and the pre-stated no-regression rule refuses them. Ground truth was not touched. (3) DID THE CONTROLS CATCH ME: twice. The pre-bash hook denied a heredoc carrying backslashes while I was adding an edge to a Decision file, which is D0309 firing exactly as designed; and clippy's too-many-lines refused the function I had grown, which forced the extraction."; }
    // RAN: keel suite 570 passed 0 failed (receipt 91238ffbf2c6); recall_bench.py 49/50@13 and --hops 2 22/50; recall_ab.py 7/8 x3; validate 674; guard ALL PASS; clippy clean
