    part recallSecondHopCloseOutGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "2d502f35-9b63-4239-8bb9-6724c5d018b6"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "018315ace003b7751ab5cb31f5ab653f2faa58bf"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }
    verification recallSecondHopRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "6b79ff58-e49c-45ae-8bd9-5ed218f4162d"; :>> title = "Sprint 593 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN HELD. Two new items, both recorded with resolvers. issue405: six configurations returned identical numbers and that neutrality is not a result but the set declining to answer - read as a result it licenses either fitting to the hand set or discarding a working mechanism, and D0325 did the second to the rare-term narrowing on exactly this evidence; a sweep must now state COULD NOT CHOOSE rather than leave a silence the reader fills in. issue406, and this one is mine: I ran recall_ab.py while the linker was still settling the image and got 6/8, one step after refactoring the very function under measurement - the obvious reading was that my refactor had broken it, and the only reasons I did not act on that reading were the latency line and re-running. It is the issue386 family arriving in the measurement harnesses. Already tracked, no new item: issue391 keeps its open definition question, now less urgent because the bar was cleared without it; issue394 keeps its open half. The lesson worth carrying past both: when a benchmark says nothing at every setting, the first hypothesis should be that the benchmark cannot see the thing, not that the thing does nothing."; }
    // RAN: keel suite 570 passed 0 failed (receipt 91238ffbf2c6); recall_bench.py 49/50@13 and --hops 2 22/50; recall_ab.py 7/8 x3; validate 674; guard ALL PASS; clippy clean
